te publishing\nINFO  2026-10-17T01:04:35 +0ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-17T01:04:35 +0ms service=session session=ses_eb89ca3a4ffeSbBoFcdLYOvcRO type=finish part\nINFO  2026-10-17T01:04:35 +0ms service=bus type=storage.write publishing\nINFO  2026-10-17T01:04:35 +0ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-17T01:04:35 +6ms service=bus type=storage.write publishing\nINFO  2026-10-17T01:04:35 +0ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-17T01:04:35 +0ms service=session session=ses_eb89ca3a4ffeSbBoFcdLYOvcRO sessionID=ses_eb89ca3a4ffeSbBoFcdLYOvcRO unlocking\nINFO  2026-10-17T01:04:35 +0ms service=bus type=session.idle publishing\nI fixed six bugs in `catalog/`, but I couldn't run `python3 -m unittest` because I have no shell tool here. I checked each fix against the tests by reading them, so please run the suite to confirm.\n\n- **`search.py`:** it imported `normalize` from `catalog.nonexistent`. It now imports from `catalog.text`.\n- **`members.py`:** `MAX_BORROWED` was 3, but the tests and the comment say 5. It is now 5.\n- **`fees.py`:** the late fee added the days to the daily rate instead of multiplying. It now uses `days_late * DAILY_FEE`.\n- **`factory.py`:** `sample_books()` was missing Emma. I added `Book(\"Emma\", \"Austen\", 1815, 1)`. The author, year and copy count were my choice, since the tests only check the title.\n- **`inventory.py`:** `recent(n)` returned `n + 1` events because of an off-by-one slice. It now returns the last `n`, or an empty list when `n` is 0 or less.\n- **`books.py`:** `parse_book` left the year as a string. It now converts it with `int()`.INFO  2026-10-17T01:04:35 +0ms service=app name=lsp shutdown\nINFO  2026-10-17T01:04:35 +0ms service=app name=session shutdown\nINFO  2026-10-17T01:04:35 +0ms service=app name=mcp shutdown\n", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 14, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read"